# NPDUs on one network: no addresses, no hop count (§6.2). Each record is a
# datagram after its datalink header; the meaning spells the APDU inside.

# Who-Is to every network: DNET X'FFFF', DLEN 0, hop count 255.
01 20 ff ff 00 ff 10 08 => to global, hops 255; unconfirmed-request service 8
# Who-Is for instances 0–1000, on this network only.
01 00 10 08 09 00 1a 03 e8 => local; unconfirmed-request service 8 body 09001a03e8
# I-Am: device 599, max APDU 1476, no segmentation, vendor 260.
01 00 10 00 c4 02 00 02 57 22 05 c4 91 03 22 01 04 => local; unconfirmed-request service 0 body c4020002572205c49103220104
# ReadProperty device 599 object-name; a confirmed request expects a reply.
01 04 00 05 01 0c 0c 02 00 02 57 19 4d => expects-reply; confirmed-request invoke 1 service 12 max-apdu 1476 segments unspecified body 0c02000257194d
# Its Complex-ACK: object-name "Lift1".
01 00 30 01 0c 0c 02 00 02 57 19 4d 3e 75 06 00 4c 69 66 74 31 3f => local; complex-ack invoke 1 service 12 body 0c02000257194d3e7506004c696674313f
# WriteProperty acknowledged.
01 00 20 02 0f => local; simple-ack invoke 2 service 15
# ReadProperty refused: error class property (2), code unknown-property (32).
01 00 50 03 0c 91 02 91 20 => local; error invoke 3 service 12 body 91029120
# Each network priority (§6.2.2, bits 1–0).
01 01 10 08 => priority urgent; unconfirmed-request service 8
01 02 10 08 => priority critical-equipment; unconfirmed-request service 8
01 03 10 08 => priority life-safety; unconfirmed-request service 8
